title: Workers' Government in Saxony
subtitle: The left SPD in Saxony offers the KPD seats in the state government.
new-page: true
tags: rf_event
view-if: year = 1923 and month >= 10
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: saxony_seen = 1

= Workers' Government in Saxony

Erich Zeigner, the left <span class="p-spd">SPD</span> minister-president of Saxony, invites the <span class="p-kpd">KPD</span> into his government. In neighbouring Thuringia a similar offer is on the table. [? if october_plan : The plan for October counts on these states: Communist ministers could open police arsenals to the Proletarian Hundreds. ?] The <span class="p-reichswehr">Reichswehr</span> is watching.

- @enter
- @stay_out

@enter
title: Enter the government.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-right">Right</span> and Moscow. Angers the <span class="f-left">Left</span> and <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span>. Legal arms for the Hundreds.
on-arrival: {!
Q.workers_govt = 1;
window.RF.lean(Q, {right: 4, left: -3, ultra: -4});
Q.moscow_trust += 3;
Q.readiness += 8;
Q.spd_relation += 8;
!}

On 10 October, Communist ministers join the Saxon government[? if leader == "right" : , Brandler himself among them ?]. Thuringia follows a few days later. The Proletarian Hundreds are legal in both states. In Berlin, the Reich government and the army command begin to discuss intervention.

@stay_out
title: Stay out of a coalition with reformists.
subtitle: Pleases the <span class="f-left">Left</span> and <span class="f-ultra">Ultra-Left</span>. Angers the <span class="f-right">Right</span>. Moscow is displeased.
on-arrival: {!
Q.workers_govt = 0;
window.RF.lean(Q, {left: 3, ultra: 3, right: -5});
Q.spd_relation -= 6;
Q.moscow_trust -= 4;
!}

The party stays out. Zeigner governs alone, and Moscow's planners lose their base in central Germany.
